═══════════════════════════════════════
TECH STACK — USE EXACTLY THESE
═══════════════════════════════════════
- Flutter / Dart
- provider:                       → All state management
- hive_flutter:                   → Local storage (progress, stars)
- go_router:                      → Navigation
- audioplayers:                   → Sound effects
- lottie:                         → Animations
- google_fonts:                   → Typography (Nunito)

DO NOT use:
- Riverpod (use Provider only)
- GetX
- setState in game logic (only in leaf UI widgets if unavoidable)
- Bloc/Cubit
- freezed or build_runner (write copyWith manually)
- Any maze or game engine packages

═══════════════════════════════════════
CODING RULES — ALWAYS FOLLOW THESE
═══════════════════════════════════════
1. MODELS
   - All models are immutable with manual copyWith()
   - All models have toJson() and fromJson() written manually (no code generation)
   - Use enums for Direction: up, down, left, right, none

2. STATE MANAGEMENT
   - All game logic lives in GameNotifier (StateNotifier)
   - UI only reads state and calls notifier methods — no logic in widgets
   - Use ConsumerWidget / ConsumerStatefulWidget throughout

3. RENDERING
   - All maze drawing is done via CustomPainter — never use image assets for the grid
   - MazePainter.shouldRepaint() must be optimized — only repaint on path change
   - Cell size is always calculated dynamically to fit the available screen space

4. GAME ENGINE
   - PathTracingController is pure Dart — zero Flutter dependencies
   - MazeSolver uses DFS and must return null if unsolvable
   - LevelBuilder must verify solvability before returning a Level (max 10 retries)

5. NAVIGATION
   - Use go_router exclusively
   - Routes: / (home), /levels (level select), /game/:levelId (game screen)

6. PERFORMANCE
   - Avoid rebuilding the entire widget tree on every path step
   - Use select() in Riverpod to watch only specific state fields
   - Canvas operations must use save() / restore() properly

7. NAMING CONVENTIONS
   - Files: snake_case
   - Classes: PascalCase
   - Variables/methods: camelCase
   - Constants: kCamelCase (e.g. kCellSize)
   - Private fields: _camelCase

═══════════════════════════════════════
VISUAL DESIGN SYSTEM
═══════════════════════════════════════
All colors and styles must come from app_theme.dart.
Never hardcode colors or font sizes inline.

Color palette:
  kBackgroundColor   = #F5ECD7   (warm cream)
  kCellColor         = #C49A6C   (warm tan)
  kPathColor         = #4A90D9   (blue)
  kStartColor        = #5DB075   (green)
  kEndColor          = #E05C5C   (red)
  kArrowColor        = #8B5E3C   (dark brown)
  kInactiveColor     = transparent
  kStarColor         = #F5C518   (gold)
  kTextPrimary       = #3E2A1A   (dark brown)

Typography:
  - All text uses GoogleFonts.nunito
  - Title: 28sp, bold
  - Level number: 20sp, semibold
  - Button: 16sp, bold

Dimensions:
  - Cell padding: 4px
  - Cell corner radius: 6px
  - Arrow stroke width: 2.5px
  - Arrowhead size: 6px triangle

═══════════════════════════════════════
LEVEL JSON FORMAT
═══════════════════════════════════════
Every level must follow this exact schema:

{
  "id": "pack1_level1",
  "name": "Level 1",
  "shape": "grid",
  "gridWidth": 10,
  "gridHeight": 10,
  "difficulty": 1,
  "pack": 1,
  "startX": 0,
  "startY": 0,
  "endX": 9,
  "endY": 9,
  "grid": [
    [
      { "x": 0, "y": 0, "direction": "right", "isActive": true, "isStart": true, "isEnd": false },
      ...
    ],
    ...
  ]
}

Direction values must be exactly: "up", "down", "left", "right", "none"

═══════════════════════════════════════
WHEN CURSOR GENERATES CODE
═══════════════════════════════════════
- Always place files in the correct folder per the architecture above
- Always add relevant imports at the top of every file
- Always write a brief comment at the top of each file explaining its purpose
- If a method is longer than 40 lines, split it into smaller private methods
- After generating any model, immediately generate its fromJson/toJson
- After generating any StatNotifier, immediately wire it as a Provider at the bottom of the same file
- Never leave TODO comments — implement everything fully
- If something is genuinely complex, add a // EXPLANATION: comment inline